      "GLINDA: She brings you good news. Or haven't you heard?\nDOROTHY: It really was no miracle. What happened was just this:",
      "DOROTHY: I thought you said she was dead.\nGLINDA: That was her sister -- the Wicked Witch of the East. This is the Wicked Witch of the West. And she's worse than the other one was.",
      "GLINDA: It's too late! There they....\nDOROTHY: Oh!",
      "DOROTHY: I'm frightened, I'm frightened, Auntie Em -- I'm frightened!\nAUNTIE EM: Dorothy -- Dorothy -- where are you? It's me -- it's Auntie Em. We're trying to find you. Where are you?\nDOROTHY: I -- I'm here in Oz, Auntie Em. I'm locked up in the Witch's castle....and I'm trying to get home to you, Auntie Em! Oh, Auntie Em, don't go…",
      "WINKIES: Hail! Hail to Dorothy -- The Wicked Witch is dead!\nDOROTHY: You mean, you're...you're all happy about it?"
    ]
